course: dictionary
lesson: 12981
title: A medical word: expectoration
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to a special field, such as medicine. You can often work out their meaning from the words around them. «The doctor listened to her chest and asked about her expectoration.» Doctor and chest are clues that this is about someone who is ill.
explain: Look for the words that help most. «The nurse gave him medicine to help his expectoration.» Medicine and help show that expectoration is something the body does when you are ill, and that the medicine makes it easier.
explain: Expectoration is a formal word, so it sounds grand. To check your meaning, swap in the everyday words coughing up and spitting out. «The nurse gave him medicine to help his coughing up and spitting out» is clumsy, but it still makes sense, so the meaning is right.
fact: «Expectoration» is a formal, medical noun.
fact: It means coughing up and spitting out mucus (phlegm) from the chest and throat.
fact: More generally, it is a formal word for spitting.
fact: Doctors use it when a patient has a chest infection or a cold.
fact: Old signs said «No expectoration» to stop people spitting, because spitting spreads germs.
exercise: «The doctor asked how often he had expectoration when he coughed.» What does expectoration mean here? | Taking deep breaths of fresh air | Drinking lots of warm water | Sneezing into a tissue | *Coughing up and spitting out mucus
exercise: A bus sign says «No expectoration». Why do you think it is there? | *To stop people spitting, which spreads germs | To show where the next stop is | To tell people the bus is free | To invite people to sing on the bus
exercise: Doctors call the coughing up of mucus by which word? | *expectoration | yawning | wheezing | sneezing
test: «The doctor listened to her chest and asked about her expectoration.» Which clue helps you most? | *doctor | asked | her | about
test: Which everyday words could replace expectoration in a simple sentence? | blinking and smiling | yawning and stretching | *coughing up and spitting out mucus | sneezing and wiping your nose
exam: What is the best meaning of expectoration? | Breathing deeply after exercise | A loud sneeze | *Coughing up and spitting out mucus from the chest and throat | A type of medicine tablet
